{#
  Props:  @comment-budget-ignore
    id         string  Id of the panel. The trigger names it in aria-controls.
    tone       string  light or chrome. Light by default. Chrome is the dark panel of the sidebar.
    align      string  end, start or stretch. The edge of the trigger that the panel lines up with. End by default.
    direction  string  down or up. Where the panel opens. Down by default.
    size       string  sm, md or lg. The width of the panel. Without it the panel fits its items.
    density    string  compact, flush or roomy. The padding of the panel. Compact by default. Flush has none and clips its content.
    as         string  The element of the panel, div by default. A form, a nav or a span are fine.
    panel      map     Attributes of the panel element, such as method and action of a form, or aria-label of a nav.
    open       bool    Shows the panel. Only the styleguide uses it.
  Blocks:
    trigger    The button that opens the panel. It carries data-popover-target="trigger", data-action="click->popover#toggle",
               aria-expanded="false" and aria-controls with the id of the panel.
    content    The panel. Use Ds:MenuItem, Ds:MenuHeading and Ds:MenuDivider, or any markup.
  Any other attribute, class included, is passed to the root element, which holds the popover controller.
#}
{%- props id, tone = 'light', align = 'end', direction = 'down', size = null, density = 'compact', as = 'div', panel = {}, open = false -%}
{%- set modifiers = [
    'light' != tone ? 'lp-menu--' ~ tone,
    'end' != align ? 'lp-menu--' ~ align,
    'down' != direction ? 'lp-menu--' ~ direction,
    size ? 'lp-menu--' ~ size,
    'compact' != density ? 'lp-menu--' ~ density,
]|filter(modifier => modifier) -%}
<div{{ attributes.defaults({class: ('lp-menu ' ~ modifiers|join(' '))|trim, 'data-controller': 'popover'}) }}>
    {%- block trigger %}{% endblock -%}
    <{{ as }}{% for name, value in panel %} {{ name }}="{{ value }}"{% endfor %} class="lp-menu__panel" id="{{ id }}" data-popover-target="panel"{% if not open %} hidden{% endif %}>{% block content %}{% endblock %}</{{ as }}>
</div>
